    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/OwedDebtItem.tsx",
      "content": "A successful save only sets a focus flag and unlocks other debts; it never replaces the outstanding-debt presentation. DebtForm's saved view renders only responses or decline text, so the resolved item still says “Reflection owed” with its old due status and lacks the required “Deferred, answered”/“Declined later” label and resolution time until the page is reloaded. Retain the resolved payload and render the settled narrative locally, removing the owed/due status without rereading the Trade.",
      "existing_code": "  const resolved = () =\u003e {\n    setWasResolved(true);\n    onResolved();\n  };",
      "start_line": 47,
      "end_line": 50,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/OwedDebtItem.tsx",
      "content": "The new editable DebtForm is not connected to the shell's unsaved-work tracking. Unlike the Review host, this host omits onDirtyChange, and TradeDetail has no callback wired to updates.setUnsaved in main.tsx. Consequently, a waiting update's Reload button remains enabled while reflection answers or a decline reason are entered (including from another tab), allowing an update to discard them. Thread the dirty-state callback through TradeDetail/JournalSection and pass it to DebtForm, clearing it on save, cancel, or unmount.",
